    "question_id": "Q3.4",
    "class": 12,
    "subject": "biology",
    "chapter_number": 3,
    "chapter_name": "human reproduction",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "Write two major functions each of testis and ovary.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Functions of the Testis:\n(a) They produce male gametes called spermatozoa by the process of spermatogenesis.\n(b) The leydig cells of the seminiferous tubules secrete the male sex hormone called testosterone. Testosterone aids the development of secondary sex characteristics in males.\nFunctions of the ovary:\n(a) They produce female gametes called ova by the process of oogenesis.\n(b) The growing Graffian follicles secrete the female sex hormone called estrogen. Estrogen aids the development of secondary sex characteristics in females.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "The testis produces spermatozoa and testosterone, while the ovary produces ova and estrogen.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
