    "class": 12,
    "subject": "biology",
    "chapter_number": 3,
    "chapter_name": "human reproduction",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "Name the hormones involved in regulation of spermatogenesis.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Follicle-stimulating hormones (FSH) and luteinizing hormones (LH) are secreted by gonadotropin releasing hormones from the hypothalamus. These hormones are involved in the regulation of the process of spermatogenesis. FSH acts on sertoli cells, whereas LH acts on leydig cells of the testis and stimulates the process of spermatogenesis.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, FSH and LH are crucial for spermatogenesis.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
