      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Spermiogenesis: It is the process of transforming spermatids into matured spermatozoa or sperms. Spermiation: It is the process when mature spermatozoa are released from the sertoli cells into the lumen of seminiferous tubules.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Therefore, spermiogenesis transforms spermatids into sperm, while spermiation releases them.",
