    "chapter_number": 3,
    "chapter_name": "human reproduction",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "What are the major functions of male accessory ducts and glands?",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The male accessory ducts are vasa efferentia, epididymis, vas deferens, and rete testis. They play an important role in the transport and temporary storage of sperms. On the contrary, male accessory glands are seminal vesicles, prostate glands, and bulbourethral glands. These glands secrete fluids that lubricate the reproductive system.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Therefore, these ducts and glands are essential for sperm transport and lubrication.",
